    <section id="scope"><h2>1. Scope and contact</h2><p>This notice explains how personal information is handled through INVOIZ accounts, shopping, seller applications, delivery operations and support. It covers buyers, sellers, applicants and delivery or logistics users whose information is provided to the platform.</p><p>For a privacy question or request, contact INVOIZ Support at <a href="mailto:{{ config('support.email') }}">{{ config('support.email') }}</a> and identify the account or transaction concerned. We may need to verify your identity before disclosing or changing personal information.</p></section>
    <section id="information"><h2>2. Information we handle</h2><p>The information involved depends on the features you use:</p><ul><li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> names, email address, phone number, login credentials, profile image and profile details you provide, such as a birth date.</li><li><strong>Orders and delivery:</strong> products, quantities, prices, discounts, recipient details, delivery addresses, order history, tracking events and delivery verification records.</li><li><strong>Payments and settlement:</strong> payment method, amounts, transaction references, GCash receipt images, seller receiving details, escrow deposit evidence and remittance records. A receipt image can contain a sender's name, number or other financial details.</li><li><strong>Applications and verification:</strong> business, identity, licensing, vehicle or supporting documents required for the seller or logistics role you apply for.</li><li><strong>Messages and support:</strong> conversations, reviews, complaints, uploaded evidence and account-deletion or restoration requests.</li><li><strong>Technical and operational records:</strong> session identifiers, IP addresses, browser or device details and security or activity logs. Where an enabled delivery feature supplies location information, it is used for the relevant delivery or tracking activity.</li></ul><p>Do not upload GCash PINs, passwords, OTPs, unrelated account balances or other unnecessary private information. Check screenshots before submitting them.</p></section>
    <section id="purposes"><h2>3. Why information is used</h2><p>INVOIZ uses relevant information to create and authenticate accounts, assess applications, process orders, arrange deliveries, check payment evidence, settle payouts, provide tracking, handle returns and disputes, respond to support requests and protect the service against misuse.</p><p>Processing must have an applicable lawful basis, such as carrying out a transaction or service you request, meeting a legal obligation, a legitimate purpose with appropriate safeguards, or your consent where required. Information should be relevant to that purpose rather than collected or used without limit.</p></section>
    <section id="sharing"><h2>4. Who receives information</h2><p>Relevant information is shared with the participants who need it to perform their role:</p><ul><li>Sellers receive the buyer and order information needed to fulfill and support their own orders, including the GCash receipt submitted for that store.</li><li>Assigned delivery partners and logistics hubs receive the contact, address, parcel and tracking information needed to move and deliver the order.</li><li>Authorized administrators and support staff access records needed for verification, settlement, security and dispute resolution.</li><li>Service providers may process information needed to operate hosting, email, authentication or other enabled features. Payment providers handle transfers made through their own services.</li><li>Information may be disclosed to competent authorities where required or otherwise permitted by applicable law.</li></ul><p>Public listings and reviews can be visible to other visitors. Private order records and payment evidence are not intended as public content. A seller's receiving QR and account name are shown to buyers for payment; avoid putting unrelated private information in that image.</p></section>
    <section id="cookies"><h2>5. Cookies, browser storage and external services</h2><p>The website uses cookies and browser storage for sessions, sign-in, security and interface preferences such as navigation state. Blocking these can affect sign-in and other features.</p><p>Some pages load external fonts, scripts, maps or sign-in features. Those providers may receive technical request information, such as an IP address, and apply their own privacy notices. Opening GCash or another external service takes you into that provider's service; review its receiving details and privacy terms separately.</p></section>
    <section id="retention"><h2>6. Retention, account deletion and archiving</h2><p>Information is retained as needed for the relevant service and legitimate accounting, security, dispute-resolution or legal requirements. Different records can need different retention periods. A privacy or erasure request is reviewed separately from closing an account.</p><p>Buyers can submit an account-deletion request in account settings and cancel it during the 30-day grace period. Outstanding orders, deliveries, refunds, disputes or financial obligations can place that request on hold.</p><p>{{ config('account_deletion.retention_notice') }}</p><p>Account closure therefore does not mean that every associated record is immediately erased. Contact support if you want a review of particular personal information that is no longer needed, or need an explanation of why a record is retained.</p></section>
    <section id="security"><h2>7. Keeping information safe</h2><p>Access controls and verification processes help restrict private records to the relevant users and authorized staff. No online service or transmission can be guaranteed completely secure. Report suspected unauthorized access or a wrongly disclosed receipt promptly.</p><p>Use a unique password, keep verification codes private and sign out on shared devices. Send payment evidence only through the intended upload or support channel, and never share your GCash PIN or OTP.</p></section>
    <section id="rights"><h2>8. Your privacy rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law and its conditions, you may ask to be informed about processing, access or correct your personal information, object to processing, request blocking or erasure, withdraw consent where consent is the basis, or request portability where applicable. You may also raise a complaint with the National Privacy Commission.</p><p>Send requests to <a href="mailto:{{ config('support.email') }}">{{ config('support.email') }}</a> with enough information to locate the relevant account or record. Do not send your password or OTP. Some requests may be limited by legal retention requirements, the rights of others or unresolved transactions; support can explain the applicable reason.</p><p>For the official explanation of these rights and their conditions, visit the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/data-subject-rights/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Privacy Commission's data subject rights page</a>.</p></section>
    <section id="updates"><h2>9. Updates to this notice</h2><p>Changes to this notice will appear here with an updated date. Use the contact above if a change is unclear or you need more information about a particular processing activity. Read our <a href="{{ route('legal.terms') }}">Terms of Service</a> for the rules that apply to using the marketplace.</p></section>
